# What a build says of a package whose placed tree is missing, where `heroes
# fetch` would refuse the address it reads it from (M-package-manager step
# 5b; panel 235's R8 and R9, the coordinator's ruling of 2026-11-08 under the
# batch's recommended answer): a `file://` source outside the program's own
# repository, a program in no repository, a source reached through a link, a
# machine with no git. The build told *not placed: `heroes fetch` places it*,
# naming a fix that cannot work; it tells the verb's refusal now, with the
# verb's code and words: `fetch/address.hero`'s `judged`, over the root
# `fetch/transport.hero`'s `root_of` asks of git, the verb's own two calls.
#
# **Asked on that error path alone.** A build that reads every tree it needs
# runs no git, and neither does a package whose tree is placed, nor an
# `https://` source, nor a `path` entry: nothing is fetched (R8), and the one
# question, where the program stands in its repository, is asked after the
# build has already failed. Git writes its answer into a staging folder
# beside the placed trees, as it does for the verb (`fetch/staging.hero`),
# its lock beside it (defect 2453), removed at once, with `heroes.packages/`
# where this question made it and nothing else stands in it (defect 2434: an
# author's own empty one stays). What a killed run left there was undone
# before discovery asked any tree (`module/packages.hero`), never here.

use cli/process
use cli/strings
use fetch/address
use fetch/index_source
use fetch/staging
use fetch/transport
use fetch/verb_place
use module/catalogue
use module/reached

# The refusal `heroes fetch` would give the entry `e`, whose tree `package`
# names, for the program read under `program` (the directory of the file you
# compile as files are opened) with the catalogue's `index` line; ok where
# the tree is placed, the source needs no repository, or the verb would
# fetch it. Where no staging folder can be made, git cannot be asked, and the
# graph's own words stand.
function refusal(package: reached.Package, e: catalogue.Entry, index: str, program: str) -> ()?
    if package.unverified || process.is_directory(path: package.opened)
        return ok()
    written: str @= e.git

    if e.version.len() > 0
        written @ index_source.written_index(index)

    if !strings.starts_with(text: written, prefix: "file://")
        return ok()
    begun = staging.begun(program)

    if begun.is_err()
        return ok()
    scratch: staging.Ledger @= begun.must()
    root = transport.root_of(transport.path_tools(), folder: verb_place.dot_if_empty(program), scratch: scratch.folder)
    staging.ended(@scratch)

    match root
        .err asked => return fail(code: asked.code, msg: asked.msg)
        .ok at =>
            match address.judged(written, root: at)
                .err judged => return fail(code: judged.code, msg: judged.msg)
                .ok _       => return ok()

# A refusal's words and its code, "" where there is none.
function said(refused: ()?) -> str
    match refused
        .ok    => return ""
        .err e => return e.msg

function code(refused: ()?) -> str
    match refused
        .ok    => return ""
        .err e => return e.code

## Tests

# The questions nobody asks git for: a placed tree, a folder of the author's
# own, an `https://` source, the Heroes index. None makes a staging folder,
# so `build/` keeps no `heroes.packages/` after them.
test "a tree placed, a folder, or an address on the network asks no git"
    sum = "sha256-" + "a".repeat(64.to_u64().must())
    git = catalogue.Entry(
        name: "yaml",
        version: "",
        git: "https://git.example.org/ana/yaml",
        tag: "v1",
        commit: "b".repeat(40.to_u64().must()),
        path: "",
        sum: sum
    )
    index = catalogue.Entry(name: "json", version: "1.4.2", git: "", tag: "", commit: "", path: "", sum: sum)
    missing = reached.Package(
        alias: "yaml",
        root: "x/",
        opened: "build/selftest-unplaced/nowhere/",
        problem: "",
        code: "",
        unverified: false
    )
    folder = reached.Package(
        alias: "yaml",
        root: "x/",
        opened: "build/selftest-unplaced/nowhere/",
        problem: "",
        code: "",
        unverified: true
    )
    assert !refusal(missing, e: git, index: "", program: "build/selftest-unplaced/").is_err()
    assert !refusal(missing, e: index, index: "", program: "build/selftest-unplaced/").is_err()
    assert !refusal(missing, e: index, index: "https://index.example.org/heroes", program: "build/selftest-unplaced/").is_err()
    assert !refusal(folder, e: git, index: "", program: "build/selftest-unplaced/").is_err()
    assert !process.is_directory(path: "build/selftest-unplaced/heroes.packages")
